  "description": "Full-span heat-time map under ONE protocol: 30 s cool everywhere. Supersedes the 2026-07-30 campaign, which ran 15 s cool (25 s at two cells) and is therefore not protocol-comparable. 35 conditions = the 9x4 grid MINUS 950x400, which was measured in sweep_20260731_134414 (corner probe) and saturates BOTH instruments: laser pinned at the 0 V rail (1228 samples) and load cell clipped at 5.000 V (192 samples). 850x400 is the true edge of the envelope - clean with 1.10 V laser margin and 4.08 V of 5 V on the load cell. Corner probe also verified CC tracking at 100% for 750/850/950 at 300-400 ms, so no overshoot risk. Explicit-conditions form (grid form cannot omit a cell); order is level-ascending within each heat row, gentlest first. ~121 min. Run with --abort-on-bad-sense.",
